not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"banned","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{U}{U}","name":"True-Name Nemesis","oracle_id":"112322ad-8f66-4cd4-98a1-f425d61a69ce","oracle_text":"As this creature enters, choose a player.\nThis creature has protection from the chosen player.","power":"3","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2018-06-08","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Merfolk Rogue"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{R}{R}","name":"Volcanic Fallout","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","oracle_text":"This spell can't be countered.\nVolcanic Fallout deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Protection from a player means that True-Name Nemesis has protection from each object controlled by that player. If an object has no controller (such as a card in a graveyard), its owner is considered its controller for this purpose.","oracle_id":"112322ad-8f66-4cd4-98a1-f425d61a69ce","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Volcanic Fallout can be targeted by spells that try to counter it (such as Countersquall). Those spells will still resolve, but the part of their effect that would counter Volcanic Fallout won't do anything. Any other effects those spells have will work as normal.","oracle_id":"bd6ce147-c991-40ac-b276-65b630fad8b6","published_at":"2009-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Spells and abilities that replace or redirect damage are not affected by this card.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The \"damage can't be prevented\" statement overrides all forms of preventing damage. Damage prevention spells and abilities can still be cast and activated, they just don't do anything.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.","oracle_id":"cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
